    "english":  "Through foreign lands where the roots of the wood-apple tree\nsplit the rocky ground, and the fallen round fruits\nlie scattered like play-balls in the tangled dry grass,\nhe told you he must journey to earn wealth, O maiden of radiant jewels!\nAnd you, concealing your grief, nodded gently and said, \u0027It is well.\u0027\nTruly you acted with noble grace;\nfor it is the ancient nature of men of resolute will\nto cross perilous realms for the sake of honorable duty,\nwhile loving women endure the ache of waiting with quiet dignity.",
